{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content","id":990779,"title":"$310,000 Stretch Goal - Licensed Community Content!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T20:41:22-07:00","id":990779,"title":"$310,000 Stretch Goal - Licensed Community Content!","content":"So this is crazy enough to warrant a thread of its own:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At $310,000, we will create a Community Content section on <a href=\"http://dtrpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DTRPG.com</a> that will allow folks who adhere to our standards' guide to create and post their own Scion 2e material on a royalty basis. We will also open up Scion 2e to licensed publishing with other companies. Setting up these programs is something we have never done before, so it will take work to figure out the details, but we believe Scion will become all the richer a game line with these programs in place. </div> </div> </div>For those unfamiliar, D&amp;D has been doing a similar idea rather successfully for a year or two now under the DM's Guild imprint, and it's allowed a ton of content to flourish for that system. This is the kind of goal that could keep Scion receiving new content theoretically forever, and allows us fans to not only create our own content but receive tangible benefit from it! This also opens the door to other companies creating their own Scion content, ideally (to me, at least) porting it to other mechanical engines like FATE or something stranger.<br /> <br /> This is very exciting stuff, and possibly the most exciting stretch goal of this entire crowdfunding campaign!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",