me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wow that's dedication to the institution of marriage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:19:27-07:00","id":991552,"title":"","content":"I'm going to start by throwing out some words of caution/advise to folks as someone active in the DM's Guild:<br /> <br /> The DM's Guild was the first Community Content program I saw with DTRPG but several others quickly popped up in the following weeks. None of them were for systems I had any investment in so I didn't look them over but I wouldn't be surprised if each one has some very specific and distinct differences regarding what can and can't be published. A good example of this would be custom pantheons. I saw someone mention that they wanted to convert Gaia, Luna, and Helios from <i>Werewolf</i>. I like the idea but I will be surprised if it's allowable as something that can be sold. As I understand it, OPP doesn't <i>own any</i> of the World of Darkness (which was why everything had to go through CCP and then got bogged down when Paradox picked up the rights). If Paradox finds any World of Darkness conversions and Rich hasn't gotten the Community permission to use it, DTRPG <i>will</i> pull it and Paradox <i>could</i> have grounds for legal action.<br /> <br /> Rich said that this is the first time he's done something like this and will need some time to iron out the details.<br /> <br /> Touching on the point about DTRPG pulling titles, I've personally had a few titles pulled and received at least one polite but strongly worded e-mail about what I did and how it better not happen again. I've seen other titles get pulled as well, though I don't know what, if anything, was said to the authors (at launch, the DMG was exclusively <i>Forgotten Realms</i> and people were posting non-Realms material).<br /> <br /> The DMG operates with a nice 50% royalty for the authors and then DTRPG and Wizards split the remaining 50%. Wizards has a much larger player base (at least, I assume it does given the weekly Adventurer's League games at a lot of game stores) and also the backing of Hasbro. Rich doesn't have that kind of financial safety net so I'm expecting much smaller royalties (though I'd love for him to prove me wrong here).<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not trying to discourage anyone. Writing and idea cultivation is one of the best parts of TRPGs. I'm hoping folks avoid the errors I've made (or seen others make.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:33:16-07:00","id":991560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=991552#post991552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to start by throwing out some words of caution/advise to folks as someone active in the DM's Guild:<br /> <br /> The DM's Guild was the first Community Content program I saw with DTRPG but several others quickly popped up in the following weeks. None of them were for systems I had any investment in so I didn't look them over but I wouldn't be surprised if each one has some very specific and distinct differences regarding what can and can't be published. A good example of this would be custom pantheons. I saw someone mention that they wanted to convert Gaia, Luna, and Helios from <i>Werewolf</i>. I like the idea but I will be surprised if it's allowable as something that can be sold. As I understand it, OPP doesn't <i>own any</i> of the World of Darkness (which was why everything had to go through CCP and then got bogged down when Paradox picked up the rights). If Paradox finds any World of Darkness conversions and Rich hasn't gotten the Community permission to use it, DTRPG <i>will</i> pull it and Paradox <i>could</i> have grounds for legal action.<br /> <br /> Rich said that this is the first time he's done something like this and will need some time to iron out the details.<br /> <br /> Touching on the point about DTRPG pulling titles, I've personally had a few titles pulled and received at least one polite but strongly worded e-mail about what I did and how it better not happen again. I've seen other titles get pulled as well, though I don't know what, if anything, was said to the authors (at launch, the DMG was exclusively <i>Forgotten Realms</i> and people were posting non-Realms material).<br /> <br /> The DMG operates with a nice 50% royalty for the authors and then DTRPG and Wizards split the remaining 50%. Wizards has a much larger player base (at least, I assume it does given the weekly Adventurer's League games at a lot of game stores) and also the backing of Hasbro. Rich doesn't have that kind of financial safety net so I'm expecting much smaller royalties (though I'd love for him to prove me wrong here).<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not trying to discourage anyone. Writing and idea cultivation is one of the best parts of TRPGs. I'm hoping folks avoid the errors I've made (or seen others make.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Wise advise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:01:06-07:00","id":991911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=991531#post991531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow that's dedication to the institution of marriage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has several explanations, some of them complicated and involving previous lives, and some more straightforward, like &quot;because mom told so, and mom's word is law&quot;. Suffice it to say, this was not Panchali's conscious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:39:09-07:00","id":992021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=991552#post991552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to start by throwing out some words of caution/advise to folks as someone active in the DM's Guild:<br /> <br /> The DM's Guild was the first Community Content program I saw with DTRPG but several others quickly popped up in the following weeks. None of them were for systems I had any investment in so I didn't look them over but I wouldn't be surprised if each one has some very specific and distinct differences regarding what can and can't be published. A good example of this would be custom pantheons. I saw someone mention that they wanted to convert Gaia, Luna, and Helios from <i>Werewolf</i>. I like the idea but I will be surprised if it's allowable as something that can be sold. As I understand it, OPP doesn't <i>own any</i> of the World of Darkness (which was why everything had to go through CCP and then got bogged down when Paradox picked up the rights). If Paradox finds any World of Darkness conversions and Rich hasn't gotten the Community permission to use it, DTRPG <i>will</i> pull it and Paradox <i>could</i> have grounds for legal action.<br /> <br /> Rich said that this is the first time he's done something like this and will need some time to iron out the details.<br /> <br /> Touching on the point about DTRPG pulling titles, I've personally had a few titles pulled and received at least one polite but strongly worded e-mail about what I did and how it better not happen again. I've seen other titles get pulled as well, though I don't know what, if anything, was said to the authors (at launch, the DMG was exclusively <i>Forgotten Realms</i> and people were posting non-Realms material).<br /> <br /> The DMG operates with a nice 50% royalty for the authors and then DTRPG and Wizards split the remaining 50%. Wizards has a much larger player base (at least, I assume it does given the weekly Adventurer's League games at a lot of game stores) and also the backing of Hasbro. Rich doesn't have that kind of financial safety net so I'm expecting much smaller royalties (though I'd love for him to prove me wrong here).<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not trying to discourage anyone. Writing and idea cultivation is one of the best parts of TRPGs. I'm hoping folks avoid the errors I've made (or seen others make.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good overview and pretty accurate as to where we are right now. We have some models towards how or maybe how not to do this, with Monte's and the Pathfinder and D&amp;D versions we can review from DTRPG, and we'll be looking at those as we decide how we want to do the Community Content part. Other people's copyrights, and the relative &quot;rating&quot; level of sex and violence we would like to have Scion connected to, are two of the things we are looking at as concerns with how to set this up. It's one thing when a fan does the &quot;Scions of Batman&quot; for their own fun, but quite another thing for Onyx Path to stomp all over the Batman copyrights with this initiative.<br /> <br /> By the time we are ready for this, and we are currently thinking the Community Content initiative should be part of the release of Scion: Origin and Scion: Hero, there may be other models to follow and other kinds of royalty arrangements, so we'll have more clarity on the plan in the months to come. Thanks!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:23:35-07:00","id":992057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992021#post992021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one thing when a fan does the &quot;Scions of Batman&quot; for their own fun, but quite another thing for Onyx Path to stomp all over the Batman copyrights with this initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost reminds me of some people mentioning things in the Steam Paid Mods thing, where they pointed out that copyright can be kind of a thing. I think an example they used was...<br /> <br /> Okay, let's say a Mod creator uses Skyrim to create a 1:1 replica of the House of Elrond (Movie Version) in Skyrim. That's great, more power to them.<br /> <br /> But what happens if the mod gets put up and they start charging for it, with Steam getting a cut and with Bethesda getting a cut? Since EA has the rights to the Tolkien properties in game form, then you've got a gray area.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is, glad you guys announced this, and I'm really glad you're taking it seriously. This may be the stretch goal I'm actually most curious about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:35:16-07:00","id":992065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992021#post992021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good overview and pretty accurate as to where we are right now. We have some models towards how or maybe how not to do this, with Monte's and the Pathfinder and D&amp;D versions we can review from DTRPG, and we'll be looking at those as we decide how we want to do the Community Content part. Other people's copyrights, and the relative &amp;quot;rating&amp;quot; level of sex and violence we would like to have Scion connected to, are two of the things we are looking at as concerns with how to set this up. It's one thing when a fan does the &amp;quot;Scions of Batman&amp;quot; for their own fun, but quite another thing for Onyx Path to stomp all over the Batman copyrights with this initiative.<br /> <br /> By the time we are ready for this, and we are currently thinking the Community Content initiative should be part of the release of Scion: Origin and Scion: Hero, there may be other models to follow and other kinds of royalty arrangements, so we'll have more clarity on the plan in the months to come. Thanks!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I'm guessing rate R, roughly were the majority of Onyx Path books are. PG-13 too low, because many deities don't have mythologies that would really be PG-13, plus you have a rep for Mature Content, while I don't think you want to be producing Scion Porn, so I'm guess XXX is out too.<br /> <br /> So I'd say its most likely between R and NC-17. Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:25:44-07:00","id":992177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=991378#post991378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: pity Batman isn't in the public domain yet... XD</div> </div> </div> </div>And never will be. Warner Brothers has the resources to renew the copyrights in perpetuity, and have no intention of letting one of their biggest cash cows become public domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:07:40-07:00","id":992194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992177#post992177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And never will be. Warner Brothers has the resources to renew the copyrights in perpetuity, and have no intention of letting one of their biggest cash cows become public domain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't even need to bother themselves - Mickey Mouse is older, and Disney will NEVER let that expire. Everyone with a valuable property younger than that can just let Disney do the heavy lifting lobbying the extensions into perpetuity for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:25:52-07:00","id":992205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992021#post992021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one thing when a fan does the &quot;Scions of Batman&quot; for their own fun, but quite another thing for Onyx Path to stomp all over the Batman copyrights with this initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I brought it up. I've seen lots of different IPs on fansites and used for fan-fiction but all of it was free for everyone to enjoy. With these Community Content programs, money is changing hands and some people may not realize that Community Content does not mean the same thing as fan-fiction in this instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992021#post992021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the time we are ready for this, and we are currently thinking the Community Content initiative should be part of the release of Scion: Origin and Scion: Hero, there may be other models to follow and other kinds of royalty arrangements, so we'll have more clarity on the plan in the months to come. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're thinking/hoping about 10-12 months?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:18:19-07:00","id":992374,"title":"","content":"Where do parody rights come into this. Personally as long as the writer makes it clear that they're writing isn't official, I see no reason to object to a Batman Pantheon. Parody is a protected right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:43:06-07:00","id":992422,"title":"","content":"You're going to want to do some research and/or get professional legal counsel on that one, Omega. Some people can't take a joke and lawsuits have happened, especially if the owner of an IP decides they don't like the tone or light cast on their characters.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't touch an IP that large unless I was 1) a well-known comic and 2) made it part of a much larger &quot;skit&quot;, such as a collection of assorted comic/graphic novel characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","user":"JSM3050","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:38:03-07:00","id":992535,"title":"","content":"Is the Cthulhu mythos copyrighted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:01:49-07:00","id":992541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992535#post992535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Cthulhu mythos copyrighted?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on how you use it. The base elements are public domain which is why you see it absolutely everywhere, but if you take graphics from different sources you're stepping out of bounds.<br /> <br /> Edit: That is to say, the works of HP Lovecraft are Public Domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:02:37-07:00","id":992542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992374#post992374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do parody rights come into this. Personally as long as the writer makes it clear that they're writing isn't official, I see no reason to object to a Batman Pantheon. Parody is a protected right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warner Brothers is not going to tolerate it any capacity that makes money for someone else. Unofficial fan works are generally free. If you want to do a &quot;parody&quot; they're going to need to at least be original homage characters, not the copywritten ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:04:23-07:00","id":992544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992374#post992374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do parody rights come into this. Personally as long as the writer makes it clear that they're writing isn't official, I see no reason to object to a Batman Pantheon. Parody is a protected right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Parody rights allow for commentary on the property in question. It doesn't allow you to take Batman and make an entire pantheon from it for players to interact in a batman-esque universe. You could change the names around a bit, but by the time whatever you have in mind is legally acceptable it's not Batman anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:15:00-07:00","id":992545,"title":"","content":"Which is to say, you're not going to get to use the Scion license to sell it on Drivethru. You want to make a fan site with your Batman Pantheon write up, that's probably no different than normal fanfiction to WB/DC and they'll ignore it... probably...<br /> <br /> But selling an actual product on DriveThru isn't going to happen, and wouldn't be protected by parody rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:01:31-07:00","id":992559,"title":"","content":"That gives me a nice idea for a superhero shard though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T18:51:47-07:00","id":992674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992559#post992559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gives me a nice idea for a superhero shard though...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about Trinity, but as I understand it, Trinity Continuum and Scion will be using the same system; I fully intend to work up a crossover shard as a superhero setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:50:24-07:00","id":992765,"title":"","content":"Depending on jurisdiction, &quot;parody&quot; is a specific term which means specific things, so you can't just make a Batman Pantheon PDF and slap &quot;this is a parody&quot; on it and expect that to be okay. Unless you meet the definition of the term, WB is likely to be able to axe it. In fact, even if you don't meet the strict definition, they're probably willing to try based on the idea that they have enough money to pour into a team of lawyers indefinitely, while you (and Onyx) don't.<br /> <br /> The Trinity Continuum has three main eras outside of the core rulebook: <b>Aeon</b>, a 2120s sci-fi setting with psions; <b>Aberrant</b>, a near-future setting with supers; and <b>Adventure!</b>, a 1920s game of pulp action. Yes, it will be using the Storypath system, although the details will vary. It likely won't be 100% compatible with Scion out of the box.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:09:33-07:00","id":992775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992765#post992765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on jurisdiction, &quot;parody&quot; is a specific term which means specific things, so you can't just make a Batman Pantheon PDF and slap &quot;this is a parody&quot; on it and expect that to be okay. Unless you meet the definition of the term, WB is likely to be able to axe it. In fact, even if you don't meet the strict definition, they're probably willing to try based on the idea that they have enough money to pour into a team of lawyers indefinitely, while you (and Onyx) don't.<br /> <br /> The Trinity Continuum has three main eras outside of the core rulebook: <b>Aeon</b>, a 2120s sci-fi setting with psions; <b>Aberrant</b>, a near-future setting with supers; and <b>Adventure!</b>, a 1920s game of pulp action. Yes, it will be using the Storypath system, although the details will vary. It likely won't be 100% compatible with Scion out of the box.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you really going to dangle 1920s pulp Scions in front of us like that and then <i>not </i>make bank off of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:32:32-07:00","id":992785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992775#post992775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you really going to dangle 1920s pulp Scions in front of us like that and then <i>not </i>make bank off of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I saw <i>Mage Noir</i>, it just felt <i>right</i>. A <i>Scion</i> period piece set in the 1920s gives me that same tingly feeling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:40:35-07:00","id":992852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/990779-310-000-stretch-goal-licensed-community-content?p=992775#post992775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you really going to dangle 1920s pulp Scions in front of us like that and then <i>not </i>make bank off of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>EVERYONE gets Relic Hats. EVERYONE. Boaters, flat-caps, derbies, fedoras, just... EVERYONE needs a snazzy hat.<br /> <br /> Note to self: Look into writeup for a 1920s Scion Adventure/Shard. Use Baccano as a reference if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cu